# HGNC gene-symbol alias table (small, public) — the input-context ablation
# reads it, so it ships with the repo to keep that ablation offline-reproducible.
!data/knowledge/gene_aliases.json
# Golden-set regression snapshot — the change-control check compares against it,
# so it has to be in the repo for anyone to re-run that check.
!data/golden/
# ...but not the previous-snapshot backup the rebuild writes beside it.
data/golden/*.bak
# Input-context ablation report. The per-variant checkpoint beside it is a
# resume artifact for interrupted runs, not a result, and stays ignored.
!data/outputs/
data/outputs/*
!data/outputs/context_ablation.json
# Same reason for these two: the manuscript gate recomputes its numbers from
# them, so without them in the repo those numbers cannot be checked. The saved
# golden-set runs beside them are diagnostic snapshots, not results, and stay
# ignored.
!data/outputs/context_ablation_grounding.json
!data/outputs/baseline_repeatability.json

# HemaGuide Supplementary Table 6 (CC BY 4.0) and the head-to-head scored from it. They ship
# so the third external comparator can be re-scored offline. The downloaded workbook stays
# ignored.
!data/benchmark/
data/benchmark/*
!data/benchmark/hemaguide/
data/benchmark/hemaguide/raw/
!data/benchmark/hemaguide_headtohead.json

# --- Reproducibility bundle (2026-09-24 audit) --------------------------------------------
# Every number, figure and gate check in the preprint is recomputed from the files below.
# LLM outputs cannot be regenerated deterministically, so the per-variant caches ship; the
# small reports derived from them ship too, because verify_manuscript and make_figures read
# them directly. Resume checkpoints (*.partial.jsonl), run logs (they carry local paths),
# rendered reports and diagnostic golden-set runs stay ignored.
!data/outputs/cohort_interpretation.json
!data/outputs/cohort_interpretation.csv
!data/outputs/cohort_noverify.json
!data/outputs/ablation_report.json
!data/outputs/eval_report.json
!data/outputs/stats_report.json
!data/outputs/discordance_analysis.json
!data/outputs/analyses_report.json
!data/outputs/faithfulness_ablation.json
!data/outputs/faithfulness_real_norag.json
!data/outputs/verifier_effect.json
!data/outputs/multimodel_faithfulness.json
!data/outputs/multimodel_faithfulness_poc.json
!data/outputs/multimodel_faithfulness_gpt4o.json

# Horak-70 benchmark: derived gold table, LLM/rule predictions, and the public-evidence
# snapshots (CIViC CC0, DGIdb, gnomAD, ClinVar) the offline re-scoring needs. The Horak
# supplementary workbooks themselves (PMC author manuscript, no open licence) stay ignored;
# scripts/build_horak_benchmark.py rebuilds the table from a downloaded copy.
!data/benchmark/provenance.json
!data/benchmark/civic_assertions.tsv
!data/benchmark/horak_benchmark.tsv
!data/benchmark/horak_results.json
!data/benchmark/horak_vicc.json
!data/benchmark/horak_gpt4o.json
!data/benchmark/horak_lovo.json
!data/benchmark/horak_temporal.json
!data/benchmark/horak_sensitivity_modes.json
!data/benchmark/horak_known_novel.json
!data/benchmark/horak_civic.tsv
!data/benchmark/horak_dgidb.json
!data/benchmark/horak_gnomad.json
!data/benchmark/horak_clinvar_os1.json
!data/benchmark/clinvar_vicc.json
!data/benchmark/clinvar_vicc_rows.json
!data/benchmark/embed_ablation.json
# OncoVI published predictions (MIT). The COSMIC Cancer Gene Census CSVs that sit beside
